A||N||2||Cplensdorf||Engine Colors||||1||
Z||000000||Cplensdorf||02-23-2001||09:29 PM||||Does anyone know the color scheme of the 88 GT V6?  Specifically, are the water pump, timing chain cover, heads, block painted? Is there a color CODE for the red valve covers/intake manifold?<P>Thanks in advance.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||strdream||02-23-2001||10:17 PM||||Engine painting is basic.  Pretty much the long block is painted as if it where dipped in paint, everything is covered. Pulleys and power steering pump are often black. Intake manifold is painted as part of the long block unless it is bright aluminum. fuel system is left natural color. valve covers are painted as part of the long block unless they are fancy. If they are cast aluminum you can paint them and than sand the paint off the high ridges to make them look cool. The same for the air intake plentum. If you realy want to do it nice, don't get any paint on the ignition or wires or sensors or exhaust system.<BR>Your local auto parts store has the engine paint colors. It is just GM red or orange or what ever for that year. It's not like they color co-ordinated them.<P>Ross ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Matt88||02-24-2001||12:49 PM||||In my 88 GT the block and heads are black.  The intake is unpainted aluminum except for the top plenum which is painted red (orange?) with the ribs and lettering left in unpainted aluminum.<P>The valve covers are also red (orange?) with the ribs left unpainted aluminum.<P>It appears the waterpump and timing cover is also left unpainted aluminum and the pully and vibration damper are painted black.<P>Hope this helps.||||reg||1
